  "details": "- CVE-2026-6460: add downstream hardening: plans and portals holding values of a row type (including the row types nested in its attributes) block shape-changing ALTERs of that type; stale PL/pgSQL records and held cursors are rejected (partial mitigation, not upstream Part B; the shape lock is held to end of transaction and can deadlock with a concurrent such ALTER)\n- CVE-2026-6460: carry the upstream rowtypes_alter regression test and the rowtypes-alter / eval-plan-qual-rowtype-alter isolation specs, adapted to 9.2 (regress expected output measured on 9.2, stable build 6afb2e91, plus a hand-written nested row type section; the isolation specs keep upstream's expected output and are not run by the build)",
